{# The airline's own mark, four figures, then how to reach it.

   Where it is based rather than a second copy of its code: the country is the
   one fact here that sends a reader somewhere else, and the code is already in
   the tile beside it and in the page's own address.

   Destinations is what its hubs can reach direct today, which is the same
   number the fares strip below is the front of. Not "routes" -- an airline
   flying 3,923 of them is not offering a traveller 3,923 choices, it is
   offering the 231 places they end up. #}
{# Empty alt: the heading directly above this says "Air Canada", so a reader
   that cannot see the mark has already been told whose page it is, and an alt
   of "Air Canada" would only say it twice. The width and height are on the tag
   as well as in the CSS so the tile below does not move when it arrives. #}
<img class="place__mark"
     src="{{ cdn(config('site.static.endpoint.images') ~ '/suppliers/' ~ place.code ~ '.png') }}"
     width="56" height="56" loading="lazy" alt="">

{% include 'partials/facts-grid.html.twig' with {
    'facts': [
        { 'icon': 'fa-plane', 'value': place.code, 'label': 'Airline code' },
        { 'icon': 'fa-location-dot', 'value': place.country|default('—'), 'label': 'Based in' },
        {
            'icon': 'fa-plane-departure',
            'value': place.hub_count,
            'label': place.hub_count > 1 ? 'Hubs' : 'Hub'
        },
        { 'icon': 'fa-earth-americas', 'value': place.destinations, 'label': 'Destinations' }
    ]
} only %}

{# Both are seed data and both can be missing -- 11 of the 105 have no website
   and 6 no phone number -- so each row appears only where there is one.

   The number is text and not a tel: link on purpose. These are written every
   way the airlines write them: "800-433-7300" is a North American toll-free
   with no country code, "+91 (0)124 435 2500" carries one, and one row ends in
   a stray dash. A tel: built from that dials the wrong number as often as the
   right one, and a wrong number is worse than a number you copy yourself. #}
{% if place.url is not empty or place.phone is not empty %}
    <ul class="chips place__contacts">
        {% if place.url is not empty %}
            <li>
                <a class="chip chip--link" href="{{ place.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    <i class="fas fa-globe chip__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ place.name }} website
                </a>
            </li>
        {% endif %}
        {% if place.phone is not empty %}
            <li>
                <span class="chip">
                    <i class="fas fa-phone chip__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ place.phone }}
                </span>
            </li>
        {% endif %}
    </ul>
{% endif %}
